      "description": "Head Coach of Swimming and Diving You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Head Coach of Swimming and Diving Hot Job Ripon, WI 54971 Apply Overview Level Experienced Position Type Full Time Apply Description Ripon College, an NCAA Division III institution and member of the Midwest Conference, is seeking a Head Men’s and Women’s Swimming and Diving Coach. Reporting to the Vice President and Director of Athletics Head Men’s & Women’s Swimming & Diving Coach Full-Time | 12-Month Staff Position Key Responsibilities : Talent Recruitment: Identify, recruit, and retain top-tier student-athletes who align with the academic and athletic standards of our institution. Program Leadership & Operations: Oversee all day-to-day administrative, operational, and tactical facets of both the men’s and women’s programs to drive team success and athlete development. Staff Management: Direct, evaluate, and mentor assistant coaches to build a cohesive and effective coaching staff. Meet Management: Manage all aspects of home and away competition logistics, safety protocols, and operations. Including budget, travel, and equipment needs. Academic Excellence: Actively monitor athlete academic progress, ensuring your teams balance elite athletic performance with scholarly achievement. Qualifications Requirements: Bachelor's Degree in related field Proven experience coaching swimming and diving at the collegiate, high-level club, or elite high school level. Demonstrated track record of effective recruiting, program building, and athlete development. Strong commitment to fostering an inclusive, supportive, and competitive environment. Exceptional communication, organizational, and leadership capabilities. Candidates must have a valid driver’s license and possess knowledge, understanding, and adherence to Ripon College, Midwest Conference, and NCAA rules and regulations. For full consideration, please apply online through our Jobs at Ripon portal. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Ripon College is committed to the principles of equal opportunity and adheres to nondiscriminatory policies in employment and student enrollment in accordance with all applicable federal, state, and local laws. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
